  "findings": [
    "Pinned Cocos 3.8.8 Graphics.activeSubModel allocates 65535*32 vertex bytes plus 65535*2*2 index bytes per submodel (~2.25 MiB), even for small shapes. The scene has roughly 80 Graphics components, including masks and hidden controls; allocation depends on which have rendered.",
    "The current local two-minute exercise did not reproduce runaway GPU buffer/texture growth. Large standing allocations and entry peaks are relevant to the reported few-second exit, but no iPhone process memory/crash trace was available to establish the exact termination cause.",
    "Fire cards repeatedly submitted unchanged transforms, invalidating Cocos scene-graph state for stationary phases."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "CompactGraphics extends the engine Graphics component through the documented protected _uploadData hook. It retains native paths/tessellation/shaders/masks and uses GFX Buffer.resize before native upload to fit actual vertex/index counts. Buffers grow by capacity when needed, without resizing every frame.",
    "24 existing component factories now create CompactGraphics; existing getComponent(Graphics), colors, paths, layout and touch bounds remain compatible. Native JSB follows the original upload path; this adapter targets the WebGL backend used by TapTap.",
    "Fire sprite position, rotation and scale setters run only when their values change. Animation timing, texture phases, transforms and tints remain equivalent in sampled poses.",
    "PlatformServices uses official optional tap.onMemoryWarning/offMemoryWarning. App records version/area/time/Android level/gfx counters under [MemoryPressure] and the single local key sword-fire-last-memory-warning, retaining iOS level=null and unregistering the exact listener on disposal."
  ],
  "constraints": "No frame-rate cap/reduction, map-size reduction, terrain/collision/gameplay change or picture-content removal. Existing Cocos renderer/components and GFX buffer API are reused; no new dependency or permanent test framework.",
